nfs2se-web
==========

This project ports NFSIISE to WebAssembly and WebGL2.

Upstream
--------
NFSIISE by zaps166 (Błażej Szczygieł) - https://github.com/zaps166/NFSIISE
Its wrapper source code is MIT licensed (third_party/NFSIISE/LICENSE). The
browser platform layer in src/platform/ re-implements the behaviour of the
upstream wrapper (Kernel32.c, User32.c, DInput.c, EAcsnd.c, Timer.c,
Wrapper.c, FetchTrackRecords.c, Glide2x.c, Glide2x/OpenGL2.c) for the web.

The translated game code (third_party/NFSIISE/src/Cpp, a git submodule) is
not covered by the upstream MIT license; per the upstream README the license
applies to the wrapper source code only. This repository does not vendor it;
it is fetched as a submodule and compiled at build time.

The build copies install.win, text.* and nfs2se.conf.template from
third_party/NFSIISE/"Need For Speed II SE" into dist/files/.

So dist/ holds material that neither this project's license (LICENSE) nor the
upstream MIT license covers: the compiled translated game in dist/nfs2se.wasm
and the upstream support files in dist/files/. Whoever distributes dist/
distributes them too.

Other components
----------------
The build output (dist/nfs2se.js, dist/nfs2se.wasm) contains the Emscripten
runtime (MIT or University of Illinois/NCSA) and code from the system
libraries it links: musl libc (MIT), the compiler-rt builtins (Apache-2.0
WITH LLVM-exception, with legacy University of Illinois/NCSA or MIT terms)
and dlmalloc (public domain, CC0). The build copies their licence texts next
to dist/LICENSE and dist/NOTICE: Emscripten's LICENSE to
dist/LICENSE.emscripten, musl's COPYRIGHT to dist/LICENSE.musl and
compiler-rt's LICENSE.TXT to dist/LICENSE.compiler-rt.

@playwright/test and the playwright and playwright-core packages it installs
(Apache-2.0) are development dependencies used only by the browser tests, as
is the Chromium build Playwright downloads to run them; none is part of dist/.

The development server (tools/serve.mjs) and the cross-origin isolation
service worker (src/web/coi-sw.js) are original code of this project.

Game data
---------
Need For Speed II SE is a trademark of Electronic Arts. Neither this
repository nor dist/ includes the game data. Players import the fedata/ and
gamedata/ directories from their own Need For Speed II Special Edition CD;
the data stays in the browser's IndexedDB on their machine.
